course: dictionary
lesson: 12930
title: Evasively: dodging the question
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Evasively is an adverb. It tells you how someone speaks or acts. When a person answers evasively, they avoid giving a clear, direct answer. «I was just around,» said Sam evasively. Sam did not really answer the question.
explain: The word comes from the verb «evade», which means to escape or avoid. An evasive answer dodges the question, like a footballer dodging a tackle. Ask yourself: did the answer tell me what I wanted to know?
explain: Readers should notice when a character answers evasively, because it is a clue. The character may be hiding something, feeling nervous, or not wanting to tell the truth. The writer is hinting: watch this person carefully.
fact: Evasively means in a way that avoids giving a clear, direct answer.
fact: «Evasively» comes from the verb «evade», meaning to escape or avoid.
fact: An evasive answer is a clue: the character may be hiding something.
fact: «Maybe,» he said evasively. The word «maybe» does not tell us anything clear.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence: «did not answer clearly» should still make sense.
exercise: «I'm not sure,» said Tom evasively, looking at the floor. What does evasively mean here? | Very quickly, without stopping | *In a way that avoids a clear answer | In a loud, happy voice | In a way that tells the whole truth
exercise: Which word is the verb that evasively is built from? | explain | *evade | evaporate | excite
exercise: Ms Patel asked, «Did you finish your homework?» Jo looked away and said, «Homework is a funny thing, isn't it?» How did Jo answer? | Loudly, shouting the answer | Happily, with a big smile | Honestly, with a full explanation | *Evasively, by avoiding a clear yes or no
test: «We will see,» said the mayor evasively when reporters asked about the bridge. What does this tell the reader? | The mayor is telling a joke | The mayor is certain the bridge will be built | *The mayor is avoiding a clear answer | The mayor has forgotten the question
test: Which is the best meaning of evasively? | Running very fast away from danger | *Avoiding a clear, direct answer | Shouting with excitement | Telling a clear, direct truth
exam: Zara asked her brother, «Did you eat the last biscuit?» He said, «Biscuits are very interesting, aren't they?» Why is this answer evasive? | It tells a funny joke | It answers the question clearly | It is a question with no words | *It avoids a clear yes or no
